Description: MeshCore repeater stack running natively on Linux
 Linux systemd service running the MeshCore mesh repeater stack natively.
 All radio operations are tunnelled over TCP to a remote modem running
 pymc_tcp / pymc_usb firmware (https://github.com/itk80/pymc_usb); the
 host needs no LoRa peripheral.
 .
 Features:
  * mesh::Radio implementation over pymc_usb wire protocol v0.7
  * Full mesh::Mesh + CommonCLICallbacks repeater (adverts, ACL,
    loop detection, region scoping, remote LoRa admin)
  * HTTP/JSON configurator on port 8080 with live status + CLI bridge
  * systemd unit with ProtectSystem=strict + StateDirectory
  * Identity persistence inside /etc/Meshcore-Linux/config.json
    (atomic, preserved across upgrades and reinstalls)
